			<div class="content" id="post-content-4521389">
									

<p>Very few things manage to incite dread properly. You need to be cognizant of the possible ending, and there can't be any subversions along the way. As a consequence, the plot often feels too obvious when not done correctly.</p>
<p>I am, pleased to say, however, that this piece handles dread wonderfully. We are made aware of what is to come, and yet, we remain curious enough to keep reading. That alone, in my opinion, deserves an upvote - and the article fails convince me to vote otherwise.</p>
<p>Great work.</p>

